<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75874" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔλω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖλος</span>
		A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be whole</i> or
				<i>sound</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ γὰρ οὔλειν ὑγιαίνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					14.1.6
				</span></i>
			), used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> in imper. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖλε</span>, as a
			salutation, <i>health to thee</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖλέ
				τε καὶ μάλα χαῖρε</span>
			<i>health</i> and joy <i>be with thee</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.402
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				466
			</span></i>:— a form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλέω</span></b>  is cited by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλείοιεν: ἐν ὑγείᾳ
			φυλάσσοιεν</span>) and Greg. Cor.<i><span class="en">
				p.491S.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
